Implement user story SKY-002-test: Vitest tests for SkyscannerClient with mocked fetch

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests covering all SkyscannerClient behaviors — constructor validation, searchFlights success, HTTP error rejection, parse error rejection, and mock mode — using a mocked global fetch so no real network calls occur.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/skyscanner/client.test.ts uses vitest and mocks the global fetch (vi.fn or vi.stubGlobal) — no real network calls are made in any test
- Tests cover constructor apiKey validation: explicit key provided, env var fallback, both absent throws, empty-string key throws
- Tests cover searchFlights: successful response returning FlightResult[], HTTP 4xx/5xx rejection with status in message (apiKey NOT in message), malformed response rejection with descriptive parse error
- Tests cover mock mode: MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture without fetch invocation; unset/empty/other values perform real fetch; no silent mock fallback on real-call failure
- vitest run exits 0 and tsc --noEmit exits 0 on the test file


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class name is SkyscannerClient, exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor(options: SkyscannerClientOptions = {}) where options has optional apiKey?: string
- Constructor apiKey resolution order: options.apiKey first, then process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY env var fallback
- Constructor throws exact error: 'Skyscanner API key is required: pass apiKey or set RAPIDAPI_KEY' when key is undefined/null/empty string
- Empty string key throws same error as missing key (key === '' check)
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env check: process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' returns MOCK_FLIGHTS without any fetch invocation
- MOCK_FLIGHTS is hardcoded array of 2 FlightResult objects with deterministic values
- Mock mode returns immediately - no fetch call is made
- Non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', other strings) perform real fetch
- Fetch URL is https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v2/flights/search
- Query params set: origin, destination, date always; adults only if params.adults !== undefined
- Fetch headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with this.apiKey, 'X-RapidAPI-Host' with 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP error handling: if (!response.ok) throws Error with exact message 'Skyscanner API error: ${response.status}'
- HTTP error message contains status code but NOT the apiKey
- Response validation: calls isValidFlightResultArray(data), throws 'Invalid Skyscanner response shape' if invalid
- isValidFlightResultArray validates: Array.isArray check, then every item is object with price(number), currency(string), airline(string), departure(string), arrival(string), duration(number), stops(number)
- No validation for adults being positive or zero - adults=0 is valid
- No validation for origin/destination/date format or non-empty strings
- No retry logic on fetch failure
- No timeout handling on fetch

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

## Banned Patterns (must NOT appear in your file)
origin/destination, from/to, apiKey not in message, apiKey NOT in message, @jest/globals, jest, SKYSCANNER_API_KEY, RAPID_API_KEY, vi.mock('./skyscanner/client'), vi.mock('../skyscanner/client'), vi.mock('./client'), silent mock fallback, mock fallback, MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='false', MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API=false, MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API=1, MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API=yes, cheapest, search/cheapest, v1/flights, skyscanner.com, x-rapidapi-key lowercase, x-rapidapi-host lowercase, Authorization header, Bearer

